    "summary": "A short notice for people who use CROP through their employer.",
    "body": "## Who operates this app?\n\nCROPwms is provided by Strattegee Pty Ltd. Your employer uses it to manage certain work information. Your employer decides what employment records to enter and which authorised people at work can see them.\n\n## What information might appear?\n\nYour name, work contact details, workplace or role, shifts and rosters, availability, attendance or timesheets, credentials and, if your employer records it, your gender (used when a client asks for a worker of a particular gender) may appear if your employer has enabled those features. The app also uses limited login, security, diagnostic and notification information to work properly.\n\n## Who sees it?\n\nYour employer’s authorised managers and other approved people can access information according to their permissions. CROPwms personnel and service providers may access limited information when needed to operate, secure or support the service. Other workers should only see information necessary for their work role. If you work through an agency and it puts you forward for a shift at a business it supplies, that business sees your name, your agency and the shift (and, if your agency takes you off the shift, any reason it gives); your agency checks your credentials against the business’s requirements (the business sees which of its listed credentials you held on the day, by name only) and your documents and contact details stay with your agency.\n\n## What does the app not mean?\n\nInstalling the app does not itself mean that you consent to location tracking, camera monitoring, biometric checks, new employment conditions or marketing. If such features are introduced, you should receive an explanation and any legally required notice or choice before they are used.\n\n## Your choices and help\n\nFor an incorrect shift or employment record, contact your employer. For app account, privacy or security issues, contact info@strattegee.com. You can read CROPwms’s full Privacy Policy at cropwms.com/legal/privacy and your employer’s notice at \\[EMPLOYER-SUPPLIED LINK\\]. You may have legal rights to access or correct personal information held about you.\n\n## Out-of-hours notifications\n\nThe app may send shift-related notices. Receiving a notification does not, by itself, alter your employment rights or require a response outside working hours. Any legal right to disconnect continues to apply.\n\n## Display controls\n\n\\[CONFIRM APP SETTINGS: optional push permissions, supported devices, account access removal, links to notices, and how a worker obtains records after leaving employment.\\]\n"
